---
import Layout from '../layouts/Layout.astro';
import Breadcrumbs from '../components/Breadcrumbs.astro';

const page = {
  title: "Download Bootable — Linux, Windows, and macOS",
  description: "Download Bootable v0.1.0 for Linux x86-64, Windows x86-64, or Apple Silicon macOS. Includes checksums and install steps.",
  ogTitle: "Download Bootable v0.1.0",
  ogDescription: "Downloads, checksums, install steps, and release limits.",
  ogType: "website",
  current: "download",
  footerLinks: [ { label: "Features", href: "/features" }, { label: "Guides", href: "/guides" }, { label: "FAQ", href: "/faq" }, { label: "Release notes", href: "https://github.com/debpalash/bootable/releases/tag/v0.1.0" }, { label: "Security", href: "https://github.com/debpalash/bootable/blob/main/SECURITY.md" }, { label: "Source", href: "https://github.com/debpalash/bootable" } ],
  crumbs: [{ label: "Home", href: "/" }, { label: "Download" }],
};
---
<Layout {...page}>
<main class="guide-main">
  <Breadcrumbs crumbs={page.crumbs} />
      <header class="guide-hero">
        <p class="eyebrow">Current release · 27 August 2026</p>
        <h1>Download Bootable</h1>
        <p class="lede">Includes the desktop app, TUI, CLI, and write helper.</p>
      </header>

      <div class="guide-body">
        <article class="guide-content">
          <h2 id="release-files">Release files</h2>
          <div class="release-table-wrap">
            <table class="release-table">
              <thead><tr><th>Platform</th><th>Architecture</th><th>Archive</th><th>Size</th><th>Integrity</th></tr></thead>
              <tbody>
                <tr>
                  <td>Linux</td><td>x86-64</td>
                  <td><a href="https://github.com/debpalash/bootable/releases/download/v0.1.0/bootable-0.1.0-x86_64-unknown-linux-gnu.tar.gz">tar.gz</a></td>
                  <td>~24 MiB</td>
                  <td><a href="https://github.com/debpalash/bootable/releases/download/v0.1.0/bootable-0.1.0-x86_64-unknown-linux-gnu.tar.gz.sha256">SHA-256</a></td>
                </tr>
                <tr>
                  <td>Windows 10+</td><td>x86-64</td>
                  <td><a href="https://github.com/debpalash/bootable/releases/download/v0.1.0/bootable-0.1.0-x86_64-pc-windows-msvc.zip">ZIP</a></td>
                  <td>~17 MiB</td>
                  <td><a href="https://github.com/debpalash/bootable/releases/download/v0.1.0/bootable-0.1.0-x86_64-pc-windows-msvc.zip.sha256">SHA-256</a></td>
                </tr>
                <tr>
                  <td>macOS</td><td>Apple Silicon</td>
                  <td><a href="https://github.com/debpalash/bootable/releases/download/v0.1.0/bootable-0.1.0-aarch64-apple-darwin.tar.gz">tar.gz</a></td>
                  <td>~15 MiB</td>
                  <td><a href="https://github.com/debpalash/bootable/releases/download/v0.1.0/bootable-0.1.0-aarch64-apple-darwin.tar.gz.sha256">SHA-256</a></td>
                </tr>
              </tbody>
            </table>
          </div>
          <div class="guide-callout">
            <p><strong>Unsigned release.</strong> macOS is not notarized. Test with a drive you can erase. Check the drive before writing.</p>
          </div>

          <h2 id="install">Install</h2>
          <h3>Linux or macOS</h3>
          <p>The installer downloads and verifies the archive. It asks for administrator access to install the write helper.</p>
          <div class="guide-commands"><pre><code># Desktop
curl -fsSL https://bootable.palash.dev/install.sh | sh -s -- --gui

# Terminal
curl -fsSL https://bootable.palash.dev/install.sh | sh -s -- --tui

# Both
curl -fsSL https://bootable.palash.dev/install.sh | sh -s -- --all</code></pre></div>
          <p>Review <a href="https://github.com/debpalash/bootable/blob/main/scripts/install.sh">install.sh</a> first. Set <code>BOOTABLE_SKIP_PRIVILEGED_HELPER=1</code> to install without write access.</p>

          <h3>Windows</h3>
          <p>Download the ZIP and SHA-256 file. Verify and extract the ZIP. Then run:</p>
          <div class="guide-commands"><pre><code>powershell -NoProfile -ExecutionPolicy Bypass -File .\install.ps1 -Variant All</code></pre></div>
          <p>Bootable installs under <code>Program Files</code>. UAC appears only for approved writes.</p>

          <h2 id="integrity">Verify the archive</h2>
          <p>The SHA-256 file checks the archive. GitHub provenance links it to the release workflow. Neither replaces code signing.</p>
          <h3>Linux and macOS</h3>
          <div class="guide-commands"><pre><code># Linux
sha256sum -c bootable-*.sha256

# macOS
shasum -a 256 -c bootable-*.sha256

# GitHub provenance; use the archive you downloaded
gh attestation verify bootable-0.1.0-x86_64-unknown-linux-gnu.tar.gz \
  --repo debpalash/bootable</code></pre></div>
          <h3>Windows</h3>
          <div class="guide-commands"><pre><code>$asset = "bootable-0.1.0-x86_64-pc-windows-msvc.zip"
$expected = (Get-Content "$asset.sha256" -Raw).Split(" ")[0]
$actual = (Get-FileHash $asset -Algorithm SHA256).Hash.ToLower()
if ($actual -ne $expected) {'{'} throw "SHA-256 mismatch" {'}'}</code></pre></div>

          <h2 id="requirements">Platform support</h2>
          <ul class="status-list">
            <li><strong>Linux x86-64</strong><span>Raw and compressed images, Windows installers, and RAW backup. Some Windows operations require <code>wimtools</code>.</span></li>
            <li><strong>Windows 10+ x86-64</strong><span>Raw and compressed images, plus Windows installers. No RAW backup.</span></li>
            <li><strong>macOS Apple Silicon</strong><span>Raw and compressed images, Windows installers, and RAW backup. Some Windows operations require <code>wimlib</code>.</span></li>
          </ul>

          <h2 id="limits">Known limits</h2>
          <ul>
            <li>Only the latest published release receives fixes.</li>
            <li>Windows installer media supports UEFI, not legacy BIOS.</li>
            <li>No persistence, Windows To Go, DOS media, or multiboot.</li>
            <li>Only the platforms listed above have release builds.</li>
            <li>Verification does not prove an operating-system installation will finish.</li>
          </ul>

          <div class="guide-cta">
            <h2>Report a problem</h2>
            <p>Include the version, platform, interface, image, drive model and capacity, failed stage, and error. Remove serial numbers and private paths.</p>
            <a class="button primary" href="https://github.com/debpalash/bootable/issues/new?template=bug-report.yml">Create an issue</a>
          </div>
        </article>

        <aside class="guide-aside">
          <strong>On this page</strong>
          <ul>
            <li><a href="#release-files">Release files</a></li>
            <li><a href="#install">Install</a></li>
            <li><a href="#integrity">Verify the archive</a></li>
            <li><a href="#requirements">Platform support</a></li>
            <li><a href="#limits">Known limits</a></li>
            <li><a href="/faq">FAQ</a></li>
          </ul>
        </aside>
      </div>
</main>
</Layout>
